me">Czechoslovak People's Army</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Czechoslovak People's Army was the name of the armed forces of communist Czechoslovakia from 1954 to 1990.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/czechoslovakia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Czechoslovakia</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Czechoslovakia was a state in central Europe created in 1918 from the Czech lands of Bohemia and Moravia and from Slovakia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/czechs"><span class="enc-name">Czechs</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Czechs are a West Slavic people of Bohemia and Moravia, in the present-day Czech Republic.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/czestochowa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/czestochowa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Częstochowa</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Częstochowa is a city in the Silesian Voivodeship of southern Poland, on the Warta river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/caedmon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/caedmon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cædmon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Cædmon was a cowherd at the monastery of Whitby under Abbess Hild who, according to Bede, received the gift of composing religious verse in a dream.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/caedwalla"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/caedwalla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Cædwalla</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><spa